# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same values in
# Vercel under Settings -> Environment Variables for the deployment.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MongoDB  (REQUIRED for any real deployment)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All three must be set together. Set none of them and the app falls back to
# keeping rooms in the server's own memory, which is fine on your machine but
# NOT on Vercel: it runs several instances, each with its own memory, so two
# players get routed to different copies of the same game and drift apart.
#
# Set some but not all and the app refuses to start rather than falling back
# quietly — a silent fallback is the failure nobody notices until mid-game.
#
# Where to get these (MongoDB Atlas, free M0 tier, no card):
#   1. atlas.mongodb.com -> create a free M0 cluster, in the region closest
#      to the one in vercel.json.
#   2. Database Access -> Add New Database User. That username and password
#      are MONGODB_USERNAME and MONGODB_PASSWORD.
#   3. Network Access -> Allow access from anywhere (0.0.0.0/0). Vercel's
#      functions have no fixed IP, so the cluster has to accept any of them.
#   4. Connect -> Drivers -> copy the connection string into MONGODB_URI, then
#      DELETE the "<username>:<password>@" part from it. Credentials are passed
#      to the driver separately, so a password containing @ / or : needs no
#      escaping. The app rejects a URI that still has <placeholders> in it.

MONGODB_USERNAME=
MONGODB_PASSWORD=
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Optional. Defaults to higher_lower; the database is created on first write.
# MONGODB_DB=higher_lower

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redis (optional alternative to MongoDB — leave unset)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any Upstash-compatible Redis works if you would rather use one. Ignored when
# MongoDB is configured.

# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
